            <svg fill="none" height="20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-body mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
          TDEE stands for Total Daily Energy Expenditure. The meaning of TDEE is the total number of calories your body burns in a single 24-hour day across all metabolic processes: Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR, 60-70%), Non-Exercise Activity Thermogenesis (NEAT, 15-20%), Exercise Activity Thermogenesis (EAT, 5-10%), and the Thermic Effect of Food (TEF, 8-10%). In nutrition and fitness, your TDEE is identical to your maintenance calories.
        </p>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ: How to calculate TDEE -->
      <details class="group bg-canvas-elevated border border-hairline rounded-xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-semibold text-ink text-sm sm:text-base">
          <span>How do I calculate TDEE?</span>
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180 text-mute">
            <svg fill="none" height="20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-body mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
          To calculate TDEE: First, compute your Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) using the Mifflin-St Jeor formula: [10 × weight in kg] + [6.25 × height in cm] - [5 × age] + s (+5 for men, -161 for women). Second, multiply your BMR by your Physical Activity Level (PAL) multiplier (1.2 for sedentary, 1.375 for lightly active, 1.55 for moderately active, 1.725 for very active, or 1.9 for extremely active). The result is your daily TDEE (maintenance calories). You can also use our free TDEE calculator above to calculate it instantly.
        </p>
      </details>

